{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "The harsh fluorescent lights of his apartment seemed unusually bright. Mark blinked, disoriented, the familiar chipped paint on his ceiling feeling… wrong. He sat up, a strange tingling sensation spreading through his limbs. His worn-out t-shirt felt impossibly soft, the fabric almost… responsive. He glanced at his hands, noticing the slight shimmer around his fingers, like a poorly rendered texture. A wave of nausea hit him, and he stumbled to the window, peering out at the street. The cars weren't moving, the pedestrians weren’t walking, and the buildings… they were all perfectly, unnervingly symmetrical. A notification popped up in his vision – a small, floating icon with a blue border and the words \"Level 1: Awakening\" blinking insistently. Panic seized him. This wasn’t his reality. This was… a game.\n\nHe frantically tried to recall how he'd gotten here, a jumble of fragmented memories of late-night coding sessions and endless streams of RPGs. He remembered obsessively tweaking his character's stats, yearning for a life of adventure, of power. Now, here he was, trapped in a meticulously crafted digital world, a player in a narrative he didn't understand. A cheerful voice chirped from his left, \"Welcome, Player! Your quest begins now! Find the Lost Amulet of Eldoria and restore balance to the realm!\" Mark stared, dumbfounded. The amulet? Balance? He was just Mark, a mid-level accountant with a crippling fear of pigeons. But as he looked down at his now-equipped leather armor and the gleaming sword at his hip, a chilling realization washed over him. He was no longer just Mark. He was a character. And his adventure had just begun.\n\n\n\n***", "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.6729406118392944}, {"token": "▁harsh", "logprob": -1.6302294731140137}, {"token": "▁fluorescent", "logprob": -0.6109057664871216}, {"token": "▁lights", "logprob": -0